Algorithm:

Step 1: Create a list to store all permutations.
Step 2: Create an empty list to store the current permutation.
Step 3: Start a recursive process to build permutations.
Step 4: If the size of the current permutation becomes equal to the array length, add it to the result list.
Step 5: Traverse through all elements of the array.
Step 6: If the current element is already present in the permutation, skip it to avoid repetition.
Step 7: Otherwise, add the element to the current permutation.
Step 8: Recursively continue the process to fill the next position in the permutation.
Step 9: After returning from recursion, remove the last element to backtrack and try other possibilities.
Step 10: Continue this process until all possible permutations are generated.

Time Complexity: O(n! × n)
Space Complexity: O(n)


-----> Code <-----

class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> permute(int[] nums) {
        List<List<Integer>> ans=new ArrayList<>();
        List<Integer> al=new ArrayList<>();
        func(nums,ans,al,0);
        return ans;
    }
    public static void func(int[] nums,List<List<Integer>> ans,List<Integer> al,int st){
        if(al.size()==nums.length){
            ans.add(new ArrayList<>(al));
            return;
        }
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
            if(al.contains(nums[i]))continue;
            al.add(nums[i]);
            func(nums,ans,al,i+1);
            al.remove(al.size()-1);
        }
    }
}
